<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Curzola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1298">1298</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Korčula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Curzola was a naval battle fought on 9 September 1298 off the island of Curzola, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korcula">Korčula</a>, in the Adriatic between the fleets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. The Genoese admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamba-doria">Lamba Doria</a> won a crushing victory, capturing most of the Venetian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> and thousands of prisoners, traditionally including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a>, who is said to have dictated his travels while held in Genoa. Peace followed in 1299.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-curzola.jpg" alt="Battle of Curzola" width="320" height="118" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fedele Fischetti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:THE_TRIUMPH_OF_LAMBA_DORIA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
